fix(make): let verification reach a linked repository, read-only (#222)

The verify container mounted the workspace volume but not the projects
directory, so every link inside it dangled and only the repository the
container was built around could be verified, which is the one case the
target is least needed for.

I5 is that a third party verifies with no access to this system's database,
and this target is the shipped demonstration of it. An adopter's first use of
it is on a repository they linked, so that is the case that has to work.

Read-only, and asserted by attempting a write rather than assumed:
verification reads a repository and must never be able to alter one.

Measured against the deployment. Before, the link dangled and git could not
change to the repository directory at all. After, all three checks verify and
the write is refused by a read-only filesystem.

